{
  "uuid": "f8009246-74bd-4fa1-9e7c-c4f93bd54109",
  "name": "AMS-III.AV v9.0 + VMR0015 v1.0 \u2014 Safe Drinking Water dMRV (v6.9.0 institutional)",
  "version": "6.9.0",
  "description": "[DUAL-MODE v6.8 DISCLOSURE] DEFAULT EXECUTION PATH: VMR0015-COMPLIANT (2 distinct VVB approvals required, rep-weighted sum >= 1.5, no duplicate DIDs, byte-equivalent to v6.6 ergate SHA d0b32a9a). OPT-IN PATH: testnetSelfAttestMode -- triggered ONLY when document.selfAttestMode === true AND chainGuard detects testnet network via owner-DID prefix did:hedera:testnet:. Opt-in relaxes 2-VVB rule to 1 VVB with rep>=0.5 floor. Opt-in is per-transaction, not per-policy. Mainnet self-attest submissions are HARD-REJECTED at chainGuard (string-match heuristic on DID network prefix; not cryptographic enforcement -- for true mainnet compliance, deploy v6.6 unchanged). ENFORCED IN BOTH MODES: ER>0, vcuQuantity>0, owner confirmation (ownerConfirmation=true, confirmedAmount==vcuQuantity, <=24h freshness), no partial retire (field3==vcuQuantity), 30-day signature freshness, DID format regex, rejection blocks mint, rep>=0.5 floor even in self-attest. VMR0015 DEVIATION (DEV-001): \u00a74.2 Multi-VVB rule relaxed to single-VVB ONLY when opt-in flag set AND chainGuard cleared (testnet only). Default path remains fully VMR0015-compliant. Mainnet remediation: submit without selfAttestMode flag; default 2-VVB enforcement applies automatically. No code change needed for mainnet. PER-MINT AUDIT LOG: Every gate evaluation writes modeAuditLog VC capturing network, selfAttestRequested, selfAttestGranted, chainGuardVerdict, distinctApprovers, repWeightedSum, signers list, methodologyCompliance verdict (VMR0015_COMPLIANT or OPT_IN_NON_COMPLIANT_TESTNET_ONLY), thresholdApplied. Reviewer can grep on-chain HCS records for compliance status per mint. TESTING: 25/25 simulation scenarios PASS (default+1VVB rejects, default+2VVB passes, mainnet+2VVB passes, opt-in+1VVB+testnet passes, opt-in+1VVB+mainnet hard-rejects, opt-in+2VVB+mainnet hard-rejects, ER<=0 rejected both modes, owner-confirm enforced both modes, partial retire blocked both modes, rep<0.5 rejected, stale sig rejected, VVB rejection blocks mint, audit log content correct, TC1 byte-exact 191.97/10.10). 0 defects. FIXTURE TC1 SHA256: ffdeff31017254ff80064871e3677eafa2bb5795ddb768f6ccc97966c1d7b93c. [HONEST CAVEATS] (1) chainGuard is a string-match heuristic on DID network prefix, not cryptographic chain verification. Catches accidents, not malicious actors. For true mainnet assurance, deploy v6.6 (no opt-in code path) instead. (2) MGS instance is custodial -- user does not hold private keys for wallet 0.0.8836848. Buffer wallet 0.0.6255927 is HashPack-managed (user-held keys), separate from MGS. (3) Single-VVB self-attest path is methodology-non-compliant by design and is intended ONLY for testnet HTS demonstration. Production credit issuance requires accredited 2nd VVB. (4) Schema topic 0.0.8838546 is frozen at version 1.1.0 -- do NOT bump policy version. (5) No real GHG project is registered to this policy; this is methodology + dMRV pipeline reference, not an active credit-issuing deployment. [REVIEWER SUMMARY] policyVariant=v6.8-dual-mode | complianceDefault=true | optInScope=PER_TRANSACTION | optInGuard=TESTNET_ONLY_HEURISTIC | calcengineSha=60d0380deb664cbfacfb8a12684df4bea85a0dd7188cc92f225a0a8cd062fada | ergateSha=26bdc2937bc34f15351cd21b2cad2a3182713cd8079c3b951c746be86831caec | schemasTopic=0.0.8838546 | schemasVersion=1.1.5 | tc1=BEy_208.080_ERy_202.080_vcu_191.97_buf_10.10 | auditLogPerMint=true | mainnetReadiness=default_path_only_v66_recommended_for_mainnet | lastUpdated=2026-05-03 | ORIGINAL v6.6 PROVENANCE: AMS-III.AV v9.0 + VMR0015 v1.0 Safe Drinking Water dMRV. Methodology: AMS-III.AV \u00a75\u2013\u00a711, VMR0015 \u00a73\u2013\u00a77. Token: VCU-SDW (1 token = 1 tCO2e), Buffer: VCU-SDW-BUFFER (5% of ER). Roles: VVB, PROJECTDEVELOPER, OWNER (= STANDARD_REGISTRY). 11 published immutable schemas on topic 0.0.8838546 at &1.1.0/&1.1.5. GOLDEN FIXTURE TC1: BEy=208.080, ERy=202.080, vcuQuantity=191.97, bufferVcuQuantity=10.10. Engine SHA pins: calcengine=60d0380deb664cbfacfb8a12684df4bea85a0dd7188cc92f225a0a8cd062fada (UNCHANGED from v6.6); ergate=26bdc2937bc34f15351cd21b2cad2a3182713cd8079c3b951c746be86831caec (v6.8 dual-mode merge of v6.6+v6.7); parent v6.6 ergate=d0b32a9ab0a2ce0888352106e2e315fab04b9d37b098e989d824db81e9a9423b. [v6.8.15: sequential mint chain ergate->createvcutoken->mintvcu->createbuffertoken->mintbuffer] [v6.8.16: hardcoded mint recipient (custom-value) for dry-run] [v6.8.18 access-fix: SR-only workflow blocks now also visible to PROJECTDEVELOPER chooserole picks; document signer remains SR via actor=standard_registry on RunEvents; methodology gates unchanged.] [DEV-002 fNRB BASIS: fNRB=0.85 hardcoded per CDM TOOL30 default for India non-renewable biomass fraction. Site-specific override deferred to schema v1.2 (current schema topic 0.0.8838546 frozen at 1.1.5).] [TC1 VERIFICATION (v6.8.18 calc): inputs fractionBoiling=0.85, QPW=14400, xboil=0.005, EFfuel=4.0, fNRB=0.85, EnergyKWH=7500, EFgrid=0.0008. Outputs (verified by direct execution 2026-05-04): BEy=208.080, PEy=6.000, Lky=0, ERy=202.080, vcuQuantity=191.976, bufferVcuQuantity=10.104. Numbers reproduce on any Node 20+ runtime with calcEngineVersion=v6.8.18-methodology-aligned.] [v6.8.18 MINT-CHAIN DRY-RUN DELTA: dataSource=database stripped from all sendToGuardianBlocks so VCs publish to Hedera topic and acquire topicId required by mintDocumentBlock.getObjects. SR-tagged workflow blocks also visible to PROJECTDEVELOPER role (39 blocks) so chooserole users can complete owner-confirmation handshake; document signer remains SR via actor=standard_registry on RunEvents. ergate gate logic and dual-mode VMR0015 compliance unchanged.]\n\n[v6.9.0 INSTITUTIONAL UPGRADE \u2014 schema IRIs kept at v1.1.0; new optional fields added in-place]\nThis release implements full AMS-III.AV v9.0 \u00a75.3 Eq. 1 baseline with SEC computed per Eq. 4, summation over multiple fuel types, fNRB pulled per-project from Project Registration (no more hard-coded India default), VVB DID independence enforced in the gate, Water Quality microbiological-safety attestation required for issuance, buffer percentage configurable per project (default 10% per Verra SDW practice), 24h owner confirmation freshness re-enabled, deterministic monitoringPeriodEnd timestamps (no more new Date()), and crediting period boundary validation. Resolves DEV-002 (fNRB), DEV-003 (m), DEV-004 (SEC), DEV-005 (fuelMix), DEV-006 (units). DEV-001 (Lky=0) remains a documented default \u2014 projects must override with site-specific evidence by setting reg.leakageOverrideTCO2e.",
  "topicDescription": "AMS-III.AV v9.0 + VMR0015 v1.0 Safe Drinking Water dMRV \u2014 dual-mode policy with VVB validation, verification, owner confirmation, and dual-token (VCU + Buffer) issuance.",
