  "policyDocumentation": "\n\n## v6.8.2 wiring patch (Option A)\n- KYC grant decoupled from PD submit. Flow: regsend -> regreviewswitch -> kycgrantvcu (on approve only).\n- regreviewswitch conditions:\n    [0] equal: option.status === 'reject'  -> reg_reject_event   -> regrejectinfo\n    [1] equal: option.status === 'approve' -> kyc_approve_event  -> kycgrantvcu\n- NO unconditional fallback. If a document carries no decision, KYC stays denied (gate-correct).\n- KNOWN GAP: no SR-facing review block populates option.status today. Methodology-compliant\n  deployment requires inserting an SR review request block (status enum: approve|reject) whose VC\n  feeds regreviewswitch. The wiring shape is now correct; only the missing review block needs adding.\n- This dry-run cycle relies on chooserole role-join (not KYC) to satisfy monrequest's hasPermission walk.\n\n\n## v6.8.3 chooserole permission fix\n- chooserole.permissions: added 'OWNER' alongside 'NO_ROLE'.\n- Reason: SR (policy owner, isAdmin=true) failed hasPermission on chooserole because\n  NO_ROLE branch requires !user.isAdmin. With OWNER added, the SR can now use chooserole\n  to join PROJECTDEVELOPER group during dry-run replay.\n",
  "config": {
    "id": "6c696c85-deb7-45d0-9fdc-f27c31f27be5",
